Why, from [`.pr-impact.json`](https://github.com/tomer-mayara/Thermus/blob/122d65bf1f035fc195792cc083732aa05c423c58/.pr-impact.json): the existing directory gains management evidence and deletion; hosted composition binds a raw reader. Components, dependencies, registry diagrams, containers, and deployment stay unchanged.

### Architecture comparison — hosted Node server

- Previously, missing/null evidence could become ordinary through SDK normalization. Reads now retain unknown; revisions include normalized management and all existing role slugs.
- Previously, the directory had no deletion operation. It now sends one exact membership ID; normal void completion is applied.
- Only the documented 422 refusal reports unsupported/no effect. Other failures remain uncertain and throw; retries stay zero and timeout stays five seconds.
- Existing reads retain their filters, paging, and one-request transport. No application route calls deletion; S2.5-01b owns admission, authority, serialization, and last-Admin safety.

All selected tests/build gates pass. Retained file-metric and habit-hooks findings have documented reasons; changed functions meet their goals. Live proof of the new deletion operation remains S2.5-02.

Merge status: **blocked**. Required decision: independent authorized human architect approval of this candidate. No other unresolved blocker; no merge performed.

